---
title: "mint (Scallop Sui Lending Protocol)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_version: assert_current_version(version)
    q_version --> q_whitelist: assert_whitelist_access(market, ctx)
    q_whitelist --> q_check_active: is_base_asset_active(market, coin_type)
    q_check_active --> q_check_amount: base asset is active
    q_check_active --> q_abort_inactive: base asset not active
    q_abort_inactive --> [*]: abort base_asset_not_active_error
    q_check_amount --> q_calc_time: coin_value > 0
    q_check_amount --> q_abort_zero: coin_value == 0
    q_abort_zero --> [*]: abort mint_with_zero_amount_error
    q_calc_time --> q_handle_mint: now = clock_timestamp_ms / 1000
    q_handle_mint --> q_get_supply_limit: mint_balance = market::handle_mint(market, balance, now)
    q_get_supply_limit --> q_check_supply: supply_limit = df::borrow(market_uid, supply_limit_key)
    q_check_supply --> q_emit: cash + debt - revenue <= supply_limit
    q_check_supply --> q_abort_limit: cash + debt - revenue > supply_limit
    q_abort_limit --> [*]: abort supply_limit_reached
    q_emit --> [*]: return coin::from_balance(mint_balance, ctx)

    note right of q_handle_mint
        INV-001: mint_balance reflects correct exchange rate at time now
        INV-002: balance_sheet updated atomically with mint
    end note

    note right of q_check_supply
        INV-003: total supply (cash + debt - revenue) must not exceed supply_limit after mint
        INV-004: supply_limit is a protocol-configured per-asset cap
    end note
